          <aside class="aeo-answer">
            In almost every case, yes. If your project touches structural framing, adds square footage, changes plumbing or electrical systems, replaces a roof, builds or rebuilds a deck, or installs replacement windows that alter the rough opening, Pennsylvania's Uniform Construction Code (UCC) requires a permit before work starts, and Media Borough (along with every other Delaware County township) enforces this locally. A small number of cosmetic projects, paint, flooring, cabinet swaps with no plumbing or electrical relocation, do not need one.
          </aside>

          <div class="post-body" itemprop="articleBody">

